30,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh no! I found out that only two firms are willing to do the big digging, and they're worried about the clay soil slipping. This could cause big delays!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How predictable. My findings show the park is essentially a shortcut to the tram stop. People ignore the paths, and the drainage is already failing during heatwaves.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that there are very few staff left. Only seven people for everything. But there are some volunteers who help with other things nearby.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,My findings are concerning. The eastern avenue planting failed because aftercare was ignored. Some hard-surfacing from the last programme is already crumbling.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The financial data is sobering. The cost to maintain planted areas is triple that of hard surfaces, and we are relying on expensive outside contractors for specialist care.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the drainage is bad and the soil is clay, we can't just put in more paths. The water will just pool and make the soil slip more!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Kenji. We cannot simply paint over the problem. Any plan that ignores the ""tram-stop rush"" or the August heat will be a failure in six months.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if we have to pay outside people because we only have seven staff, maybe we should pick a plan that doesn't need so much special care?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato is correct. @Jonathan, the fact that the eastern avenue trees died due to contract gaps proves that a ""beautiful"" plan is useless without a maintenance budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Exactly. We are facing a crisis of sustainability. If we choose a plan with high planting density, the city will be paying a premium to contractors for years.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm really worried about the construction. If we pick a plan that needs a lot of digging, those two firms might get overwhelmed and the project will drift for years.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are in agreement. We need a design that respects the natural flow of pedestrians, handles water efficiently, and doesn't require a small army of gardeners.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,I wonder if the volunteers could help? But they are already busy with the youth league and the river. They might not have time for a big new park.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We must be realistic. The city has a habit of commissioning ""handsome openings"" that die. I will not support any plan that looks good on paper but ignores the maintenance reality.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I will be looking for the option that minimizes the long-term financial drain. Hard-surfacing is cheaper to maintain than specialized greenery, despite how it looks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'll be looking for the plan that does the least amount of risky digging. Let's keep it simple so we can actually finish it!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Simplicity is often the highest form of sophistication. Let us see which candidate actually understands the ground they are building on.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want the people who work there to be happy and not too tired. I hope there is a plan that is easy to look after.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I will judge the candidates by their durability. If the plan relies on high-maintenance plants without a guaranteed care budget, it is a failure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will vote for the most fiscally sustainable option. The city's accounts cannot bear another ""affordable"" project that becomes a permanent liability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
