58,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Plan A sounds scary because of the ponds and clay soil. Plan B is mostly paving, which means less digging. I think B is the safest for the timeline!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan A is a disaster waiting to happen given the drainage callouts. Plan B acknowledges the pedestrian flow, though it might be a heat-sink in August.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Plan C has too many trees... that means a lot of pruning and care. Plan B is just a plaza, so the seven staff members can probably manage it easily.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Plan C is a repeat of the eastern avenue mistake; the trees will die without a dedicated contract. Plan B is durable and avoids the ""short life"" cycle of city greenery.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Plan A and C are financial traps. The upkeep for wetlands and woodlands is far higher than for a plaza. Plan B is the only one that is fiscally sustainable.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, what about Plan D? It has courts and seating. But the southern side is where the hoarding is easier. Maybe D is okay too?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan D ignores the tram-stop crossing. People will just walk across the courts, ruining the surfaces. Plan B's open plaza accommodates the actual human behavior.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Kenji, Plan D has changing rooms and courts. That sounds like a lot of cleaning and managing. Plan B seems the most peaceful for the workers.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Plan D involves significant hard-surfacing, but the ""stepped seating"" often cracks if the base isn't perfect. Plan B is a simpler, more honest design.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Plan D has higher maintenance costs than B due to the facilities and court surfaces. Plan B's paving is the most cost-effective long-term solution for the city.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm sold on Plan B. It avoids the clay slippage risks of the ponds and the massive planting of the woodland. It's the most likely to be finished on time.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. It is the only plan that doesn't fight the ground or the people. It accepts the park as a transit space and a gathering point.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,I think Plan B is the best. It doesn't ask too much from the few people who have to look after it. It feels like a kind choice for the staff.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I have seen enough failed ""green"" projects to know that Plan B is the only one that will still look good in ten years. It is the most durable choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,The numbers are clear. Plan B minimizes the reliance on expensive bought-in services and keeps the annual spend per hectare at a manageable level.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Everyone seems to agree! I'm glad we checked the soil and the firms first. Let's go with Plan B!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A rare moment of total consensus. Logic has prevailed over the allure of a pretty picture.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy we all agree. I hope the people who work there like the new plaza.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,It is the only responsible choice. We are choosing longevity over a temporary facade.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am satisfied. We have avoided a future financial burden and chosen a path of stability.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
